{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1389717-mage-adventure-set-in-2020-request-for-advice","id":1389717,"title":"Mage Adventure set in 2020 (request for advice)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-18T11:57:25-07:00","id":1389717,"title":"Mage Adventure set in 2020 (request for advice)","content":"So I'm starting to write my adventure for Mage that I eventually plan to stick in the Storyteller's Vault. Yes, it's me again, and it's about tradition Mages establishing a base in the Philippines. This isn't so much something I hope to run in the near future but more like something resulting from my desire to contribute to the world of a game I really like. In short, I really want to get things right for the people who might want to pick it up and play it some day. <br /> <br /> The idea was forming before the whole pandemic thing and I was wondering what you guys think I should do in the context of writing the adventure. <br /> <br /> The easy thing would be to set it to 2015 or some date earlier or maybe to late 2020 (or early 2021) when things were more or less normal (or at least I hope they will be in 2021). I usually prefer to set my WoD games in the near future but am not really sure how things will be in like say 1 month from now. <br /> <br /> Having several representatives of the Traditions show up is a bit weird during the lockdown period too, so I'm leaning to setting the game in 2021 or at least late 2020 (November maybe?)<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T11:58:25-07:00","id":1389718,"title":"","content":"Edit: or should I be more vague on the time period? Or should I ignore the lockdown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:21:45-07:00","id":1389739,"title":"","content":"I'd say if you want to avoid Covid-19 issues but want a modern adventure, say something like this adventure is set for the years 2015 to the near present or even near future.<br /> <br /> That way you get the general cultural and technological milieu right and if someone picks up the adventure years after you publish it, the adventure is still relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T01:55:05-07:00","id":1389895,"title":"","content":"So. 2015 or 2021? Which would be better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:08:58-07:00","id":1389935,"title":"","content":"I think the past it's best if you don't want to mention Covid-19 at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:16:43-07:00","id":1390005,"title":"","content":"I would agree with the past being easier for more people to grasp. On the history, unless the adventure is really an exploration of the history of the area, you're setting a mood.<br /> <br /> So, for example, if I was to run an adventure set in the Roaring 1920s in the U.S., I'd be focused more on the bootleggers (illegal alcohol sellers), jazz and other cultural elements than delving into the regulation of the electric and oil industries for most players. All of those topics are important historically, but it would be more fun to game the non-energy tropes for most people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:38:44-07:00","id":1390029,"title":"","content":"Thanks. 2015 then. Yup. That seems about right.<br /> <br /> As for focus, it'll be kind of about the interesting highlights (less boring parts) of the history of the place (Intramuros Manila) that the mages are planning to build their base in and the mark historical events left on the present day, including possibly, the ancient spiritual significance of the spot, some summonable heroes from the past, maybe a slumbering were crocodile, and the lasting effects that WW2 had on the place (the place was virtually obliterated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:26:24-07:00","id":1390063,"title":"","content":"I recommend having some links to quality historical sources on the historical events of Intramuros Manilla so that you can give a brief snippet and direct those Storytellers with groups more interested in the history to a more rich exploration of the topic.<br /> <br /> Were crocodile? Sounds like a Mokole coming in and crossing over. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:04:44-07:00","id":1390073,"title":"","content":"That's sound advice. I should be able to add that in. The place was an ancient settlement, turned spanish walled capital fort city, attacked by the British I think, a place of revolutionary significance, modernized into a tourist attraction, taken over by the Japanese, obliterated by allied artillery, then rebuilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T20:53:35-07:00","id":1391852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1389717-mage-adventure-set-in-2020-request-for-advice?p=1389718#post1389718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: or should I be more vague on the time period? Or should I ignore the lockdown?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you set it a little bit in the past, then you spare yourself the work of creating an alternate history. Of course, an alternate 2020 will mean &quot;only&quot; a few months of alternate history, but going further into the future is setting up more work for yourself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}